{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>the meaning of מישרים:</b> they are the judgments of the Torah and its righteous deeds, given through His emissaries, and they are — <b>Moses:</b> among His priests — the word כהן throughout Scripture means one who serves: 'the priests of YHWH' = the servants of our Elohim; 'and he ministered to me' [similarly]. Therefore, although Aaron was the chief priest, Moses was the priest of priests, for he served during the seven days of ordination. And he mentioned Samuel, who was of their families, in his calling upon HaShem — and He answered him immediately, as written: 'I call upon YHWH and He answers me' (Psalms 99:6)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 99, :notes {0 "The bracketed opening appears in the source as a marginal or prefatory gloss; included as part of the comment. The verse quoted at the end paraphrases Psalms 3:5 / 99:6."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:38.057992020Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}